# Angular 21 Coding Standards

## TypeScript

- Use strict mode (`strict: true` in tsconfig)
- Avoid `any` — use `unknown` when type is uncertain
- Prefer type inference for obvious types
- Use explicit return types on public methods

## Components (Angular 21)

- **Standalone components only** — no NgModules
- Use `input()` and `output()` functions, not decorators
- Use `computed()` for derived state from signals
- Use `signal()` for local component state
- Set `changeDetection: ChangeDetectionStrategy.OnPush`
- Prefer inline templates for small, focused components
- Keep components small — single responsibility

## State Management

- **Signals** for local component state
- **RxJS** for async streams, HTTP, and cross-component communication
- Keep state transformations pure
- Use `update` or `set` on signals — never `mutate`

## Forms

- **Reactive forms** over template-driven forms
- Validate before API calls
- Use built-in validators + custom validators

## Templates

- Use native control flow: `@if`, `@for`, `@switch` (not `*ngIf`, `*ngFor`)
- Use the `async` pipe to handle observables
- Never use `innerHTML` with untrusted content
- Use `class` bindings — not `ngClass`
- Use `style` bindings — not `ngStyle`
- Avoid complex logic in templates — push to component

## Styling

- **Bootstrap 4** for layout and base components
- SCSS for component-specific styles
- **No Tailwind** — Bootstrap only
- Responsive via Bootstrap grid (`col-`, `col-md-`, `col-lg-`)
- Semantic HTML over div-soup

## Services

- Use `providedIn: 'root'` for singleton services
- Use `inject()` function instead of constructor injection
- Single responsibility per service

## Routing

- Lazy load feature routes
- Use `CanActivateFn` guards (not class-based guards)

## Accessibility

- Pass AXE checks
- WCAG AA minimums — focus management, color contrast, ARIA
- Semantic HTML (`<button>`, `<nav>`, `<main>`, etc.)
- `aria-label` on icon-only buttons

## Naming Conventions

| Type | Convention | Example |
|------|------------|---------|
| File name | `kebab-case` | `user-profile.component.ts`, `auth.service.ts` |
| Component class | `PascalCase` | `UserProfileComponent` |
| Service class | `PascalCase` | `UserService`, `AuthService` |
| Interface / Type | `PascalCase` | `User`, `CreateUserDto` |
| Method / Variable | `camelCase` | `getUsers()`, `isLoading` |
| Constant | `PascalCase` | `MaxPageSize`, `DefaultTimeout` |
| Signal | `camelCase` | `users`, `loading`, `error` |
| Template variable | `camelCase` | `#userForm`, `*user of users` |
| SCSS class | `kebab-case` | `.user-card`, `.nav-header` |
| CSS custom property | `kebab-case` | `--primary-color`, `--spacing-md` |
| Route path | `kebab-case` | `/user-profile`, `/dashboard/settings` |
| Component selector | `kebab-case` with prefix | `app-user-card` |

### Selector Prefix

- Use `app-` as default prefix for component selectors
- Configure in `angular.json` under `projects.LAP_CLIENT.prefix`

### Interface Naming — No "I" Prefix

```typescript
// ✅ No 'I' prefix for interfaces (cleaner, follows Angular convention)
interface User {
  id: string;
  name: string;
}

// ❌ Not used in this project
interface IUser { ... }
```

## Code Quality

- Remove unused imports and variables
- No `console.log` in production code
- Group imports: Angular → third-party → project

### Import Ordering

```typescript
// 1. Angular core/modules
import { Component, inject, signal } from '@angular/core';
import { RouterLink } from '@angular/router';

// 2. Third-party
import { FormsModule, ReactiveFormsModule } from '@angular/forms';

// 3. Project
import { UserService } from '../services/user.service';
import { User } from '../models/user';
```
